## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to triage, harden reliability under pressure, and coordinate cross-team remediation with business impact.

## Key Concepts

- Incident containment and rollback
- Safe fallbacks, circuit breakers, backoff strategies
- Cross-team governance and ownership
- Metrics: latency, payout SLA, MTTR, post-incident learning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: simple circuit breaker
class Breaker {
  constructor(threshold) {
    this.failures = 0;
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.open = false;
  }
  call(fn) {
    if (this.open) throw new Error('Breaker is open');
    return fn().catch(() => {
      this.failures++;
      if (this.failures > this.threshold) this.open = true;
      throw;
    });
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure success after the fix? 
- What would you include in the post-incident report for audit and compliance?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates how a manager translates reliability goals into a concrete plan, balancing speed and risk, across teams and regions.

## Key Concepts
- SLOs and SLIs for latency and errors
- Incident response and runbooks
- Canary deployments and feature flags
- Tail latency and multi-region observability
- Instrumentation, profiling, and postmortems

## Code Example
```javascript
function percentile(arr, p){
  if (arr.length===0) return 0;
  const s = arr.slice().sort((a,b)=>a-b);
  const idx = Math.floor((p/100)*(s.length-1));
  return s[idx];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you triage if p95 spikes are caused by an upstream service?
- How would you communicate risk to leadership during an incident?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a scalable reliability program that balances incident response with feature velocity and ROI.

## Key Concepts

- Platform vs product team governance
- SRE metrics: SLOs, error budgets, MTTR, and availability
- Incident playbooks, runbooks, blameless postmortems
- Auto-remediation, circuit breakers, canaries, multi-region failover
- ROI linkage and cost avoidance through reliability investments

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal auto-remediation skeleton
function autoRemediate(incident) {
  if (incident.severity === 'critical') {
    activateFailover();
  } else if (incident.type === 'timeout') {
    triggerCircuitBreaker();
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you prove ROI for reliability initiatives over time?
- Which metrics and milestones would you track to adjust SLOs?

